            <div class="entry-body">
                <h3 class="entry-title">Finnimo</h3>
                <p class="entry-context">Software Engineer Intern</p>
                <p>
                    Finnimo’s personal-finance product existed as a mobile app and a pitch. I rebuilt it as a web
                    application and added the agentic layer on top, then it went into investor pitches.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Owned onboarding, authentication, and the dashboard flows in Next.js, TypeScript, and Supabase.</li>
                    <li>Linked real bank and investment accounts through Plaid, which forced discipline about what an AI agent may do without a human in the loop.</li>
                    <li>Built an internal MCP server connecting the model to planning and investing features, with guardrails on what it could act on, and a retrieval layer so advice reflected the user’s actual finances.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="entry-stack">Next.js, TypeScript, Supabase, Plaid, OpenAI API, MCP</p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="entry" id="smart">
            <div class="entry-meta"><span>Jan – May 2026</span><span>Blacksburg, VA</span></div>
            <div class="entry-body">
                <h3 class="entry-title">SMART</h3>
                <p class="entry-context">AR Software Engineer</p>
                <p>
                    An IoT startup controlling smart-home devices through the Apple Vision Pro. The bar I set for
                    the interface was that it had to beat walking to the switch.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Rebuilt device control around spatial selection instead of menu traversal. Activation fell from about 30 seconds to 10.</li>
                    <li>Built an AR automation builder that cut time-to-automation by 30% while letting people express more complex rules, not fewer.</li>
                    <li>Integrated devices through Home Assistant on a Raspberry Pi and worked through more than ten navigation and interface flaws in the app.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="entry-stack">Apple Vision Pro, Unity, Home Assistant, Raspberry Pi</p>
            </div>
        </li>
